{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,75p' tasks/2026-07-14-M0-alignment-matrix.md\"","aggregated_output":"# AJAMIX M0 Social and Citizenship Studies Alignment Matrix\n\n**Task:** AJAMIX-M0-PREFLIGHT  \n**Declared target:** NERDC 2025 revised *Social and Citizenship Studies*, Primary 3–6  \n**Report generated:** 2026-07-14 19:48:12 EDT (UTC-04:00)  \n**Rows:** 60 (15 each for P3, P4, P5, and P6)  \n**Verification status for every row:** `BEST-EFFORT — NOT VERIFIED AGAINST OFFICIAL NERDC GRADE DOCUMENT`\n\n## Source and interpretation warning\n\nThe official grade-level NERDC 2025 Social and Citizenship Studies document was not accessible. Its LMIS delivery is login-gated, and the two public NERDC documents below confirm the revised subject, implementation principles, and grade bands but do **not** publish grade-level strands, topics, objectives, or page mappings. Consequently:\n\n- Nothing in the `Official strand / theme` column is represented as an official NERDC strand. Each entry is explicitly a **public-source topic family**.\n- The `Official topic or objective / public-source basis` column paraphrases the cited public source unless it specifically says otherwise. It does not invent or quote an inaccessible NERDC objective.\n- `Direct coverage` means a close topic match at the proposed grade in a cited public scheme; `Combined coverage` means the module combines or reframes multiple public-source topics, or uses an adjacent grade; `Enrichment` means the brief adds or relocates material beyond the grade-level public SCS scheme found.\n- NERDC 2025 remains the declared target curriculum. Every row remains provisional until compared with the official grade document.\n\n## Source register\n\n| Code | Source document | Date / version | Public location | Use in this matrix |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| S1 | NERDC, *Revised 9-Year Basic Education Curriculum Implementation Strategy* | 2025 public implementation version; exact issue date not printed in the PDF | https://nerdc.gov.ng/content_manager/Revised%209%20Year%20BEC%20Implementation%20Strategy%203.pdf | Official context only: competency framework, citizenship, cultural/global awareness, digital responsibility, entrepreneurship, environment/sustainability, gender sensitivity, SCS subject listing, and phased implementation. No grade topics. |\n| S2 | NERDC, *Special Notice on the List of Approved Subjects/Offerings for the Newly Revised Basic and Senior Secondary Education Curriculum* | 8 September 2025 | https://www.nerdc.gov.ng/content_manager/Press%20Release%20On%20New%20FG%20Curriculum.pdf | Official confirmation that Social and Citizenship Studies is a separate subject at P1–3 and P4–6. No grade topics. |\n| S3 | SchemeofWork.com, *Primary 3 Scheme of Work Unified* — Social and Citizenship Studies sections | Public unified scheme page, undated; accessed 2026-07-14 | https://schemeofwork.com/primary-3-scheme-of-work-unified/ | Newer public, publisher-described NERDC/NAPPS-aligned P3 SCS topic sequence. Not an official NERDC publication. |\n| S4 | SchemeofWork.com, *Primary 4 Scheme of Work Unified* — Social and Citizenship Studies sections | Public unified scheme page, undated; accessed 2026-07-14 | https://schemeofwork.com/primary-4-scheme-of-work-unified/ | Newer public, publisher-described NERDC/NAPPS-aligned P4 SCS topic sequence. Not an official NERDC publication. |\n| S5 | SchemeofWork.com, *Primary 5 Scheme of Work Unified* — Social and Citizenship Studies sections | Public unified scheme page, undated; accessed 2026-07-14 | https://schemeofwork.com/primary-5-scheme-of-work-unified/ | Newer public, publisher-described NERDC/NAPPS-aligned P5 SCS topic sequence. Not an official NERDC publication. |\n| S6 | SchemeofWork.com, *Primary 6 Scheme of Work Unified* — Social and Citizenship Studies sections | Public unified scheme page, undated; accessed 2026-07-14 | https://schemeofwork.com/primary-6-scheme-of-work-unified/ | Newer public, publisher-described NERDC/NAPPS-aligned P6 SCS topic sequence. Not an official NERDC publication. |\n| S7 | Lagos State Ministry of Education, *Schemes of Work for Primary School 4–6* (Civic Education and Social Studies) | Legacy public PDF; date not printed in the mirrored file | https://classbasic.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/LAGOS-STATE-SCHEME-OF-WORK-FOR-PRIMARY-4-6-1-2.pdf | Public state-ministry-branded legacy topic detail and page references. It predates the 2025 subject split and is not treated as NERDC 2025 wording. |\n| S8 | Federal Ministry of Education eLearn, teacher resources | Live federal resource catalog; accessed 2026-07-14 | https://elearn.education.gov.ng/resources/teachers/ | Public federal lesson-resource corroboration for P3 civic topics; no comprehensive scheme or stable PDF pages. |\n| S9 | SchemeofWork.com, *Primary 6 Blended British Nigerian Scheme of Work* — Social Studies | Public enrichment scheme, undated; accessed 2026-07-14 | https://schemeofwork.com/primary-6-blended-british-nigerian-scheme-of-work/ | Supplemental age-band objectives for human rights and democracy. Not an official NERDC source. |\n| S10 | *PRIMARY 4Split — 2025/26 compiled unified scheme* — Nigerian History/geography portion | Public compiled scheme, uploaded 2026; accessed 2026-07-14 | https://www.scribd.com/document/994445372/PRIMARY-4Split-20260112-1154 | Cross-subject corroboration for Nigeria’s peoples, geography, states/FCT. Used only as enrichment and boundary evidence, not as SCS authority. |\n| S11 | Supreme Court of Nigeria, jurisdiction/about pages | Live official judiciary site; accessed 2026-07-14 | https://www.supremecourt.gov.ng/court-jurisdiction | Supplemental factual authority for the Supreme Court’s apex/appellate role. Not a curriculum source. |\n\n## Alignment matrix\n\n### Primary 3\n\n| Module ID | English title | Curriculum version / actual source used | Grade | Official strand / theme | Official topic or 